uestion/math-academy-id "q-122937" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-3,7]?$\n- **I.** ${-3,-5,1,2,6}$\n- **II.** ${-3,0,3,7,8}$\n- **III.** ${-3,-2,1,3,4,7}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=7.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[-3,7].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[-3,7].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72905ab0-a733-5444-b228-2909f22d66b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462103} {:answer/id #uuid "0bba932b-ac60-5190-b246-809450ca8184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72905ab0-a733-5444-b228-2909f22d66b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462103} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bcd569-770e-5e56-999c-b6c6fea7c704" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e8fceca-ad1f-553f-b1ae-fe2c3ddb4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462105} {:answer/id #uuid "882459bb-e603-5cca-bca5-49e509a1cc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e8fceca-ad1f-553f-b1ae-fe2c3ddb4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462105} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c1ee2c-3ed9-508e-85bf-38d31fb14d69" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bfb0fa3-fc7f-5f90-b747-7ae59892eded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462107} {:answer/id #uuid "17db6afa-0a52-5a1b-b581-fb1c6a16a12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17db6afa-0a52-5a1b-b581-fb1c6a16a12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462108} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecabc5c1-9328-5f82-a212-4432161d262a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8952dce8-c604-5674-b4ed-f948b3d55e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-122938" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,4]?$\n- **I.** $0<0.5<1.5<2.5<4<4.5$\n- **II.** ${0,1,2,3.9}$\n- **III.** $0<0.1<1.5<2.5<4$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since $4.5$ does not belong to $[0,4].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is  a partition of  $[0,4].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fdb0422-e00a-5e11-8104-48d5cd25b697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254221} {:answer/id #uuid "4f652284-78d1-58c0-9b15-97c5c58fc918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254361} {:answer/id #uuid "ad834d98-f544-5531-af65-3952e32684ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255200} {:answer/id #uuid "b76d3d4d-5984-5fb6-a496-cf3192aaacfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255295} {:answer/id #uuid "c50e3528-b495-539f-a4f6-5c1029278750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b76d3d4d-5984-5fb6-a496-cf3192aaacfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255295} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a06de2c-217b-5b77-9806-05c52b3e4d9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "108d22ab-96a8-5eeb-96fd-0dcc96561441" :question/math-academy-id "q-122977" :question/problem "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $(-4)$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}=-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,10],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=(-4)\\cdot 8=-32.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141db895-bbc5-5054-af56-41c9ff81d0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253841} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd0467c-8cf6-54c1-bb7e-97ff80ee14ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254502} {:answer/id #uuid "a2bea880-8003-5c03-a805-455200652d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255106} {:answer/id #uuid "b46eba14-eda9-524d-885f-6b933077cd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255259} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e04e76-daf6-5fb9-ba27-c5ac9f640831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46eba14-eda9-524d-885f-6b933077cd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255259} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff6ccbc-1bac-587e-b4e7-254172104711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99e23ff1-d646-54b7-8668-22a06e7d8b04" :question/math-academy-id "q-122979" :question/problem "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,9].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $7$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}=7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,9],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}=7\\cdot 5=35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a21aab7-fc2e-549f-aab8-41f5bccb2b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253892} {:answer/id #uuid "507bca0f-38a3-53f7-b541-4c90fdccc251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254371} {:answer/id #uuid "b6620d40-be8d-5c18-b31f-71953ef9c8f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255285} {:answer/id #uuid "c34909b9-269b-56e5-a1c2-f53b84a64cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255414} {:answer/id #uuid "e094f232-f2ca-54f4-a9f8-04b288b09a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a21aab7-fc2e-549f-aab8-41f5bccb2b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253892} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b9846e-3490-5206-b201-c84233f5e785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e65ff59b-de1e-50f4-9c3d-679e5004d29d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122992" :question/problem "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,4].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=(-2)\\cdot 12=-24.\n$$"}]}
